@startuml
autonumber
skinparam style strictuml
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 150

actor "User\n(Host/Creator)" as User
participant "ClientApp\n(View)" as Client
participant "VirtualView\n(Client Proxy)" as Callback
participant "VirtualServer\n(Server Proxy)" as Server
participant "GameController" as Controller
participant "GameModel" as Model
participant "ClientHandler\n(Observer)" as Handler

== Phase 1: Server Connection ==
User -> Client: Start application
activate Client
Client -> Server: connect(VirtualView)
activate Server
create Handler
Server -> Handler: new ClientHandler(VirtualView, GameModel)
Server -> Model: addObserver(Handler)
Server --> Client: Connection confirmed
deactivate Server

== Phase 2: Game Creation ==
User -> Client: Enters Nickname, Color, and GameSize\nClicks "Create Game"

alt Valid Inputs (Success)

    note over Client, Server: The client sends requests to register the creator and initialize the room

    ' 1. Adding the creator
    Client -> Server: addPlayer("Alice", "RED")
    activate Server
    Server -> Controller: addPlayer("Alice", "RED")
    activate Controller
    Controller -> Model: addPlayer(new Player)
    activate Model

    Model -> Handler: onModelChanged(PLAYER_ADDED)
    activate Handler
    Handler ->> Callback: showUpdate(PlayerAddedMessage)
    activate Callback
    Callback -> Callback: executeOnClient(this)
    deactivate Callback
    deactivate Handler

    Model --> Controller: return
    deactivate Model
    Controller --> Server: return
    deactivate Controller
    Server --> Client: return
    deactivate Server

    ' 2. Room initialization
    Client -> Server: startGame()
    activate Server
    Server -> Controller: startGame()
    activate Controller
    Controller -> Model: initializeGame()
    activate Model

    note right of Model: The Model creates the Board, decks,\nsets the gameSize,\nbut does NOT start the turns\nuntil the room is full.

    Model -> Handler: onModelChanged(GAME_STARTED)
    activate Handler
    Handler ->> Callback: showUpdate(GameStartedMessage)
    activate Callback
    Callback -> Callback: executeOnClient(this)
    deactivate Callback
    deactivate Handler

    Model --> Controller: return
    deactivate Model
    Controller --> Server: return
    deactivate Controller
    Server --> Client: return
    deactivate Server

    User <-- Client: Shows waiting room\n(Lobby) successfully created

else Exception Thrown (e.g., InvalidActionException or Network Error)

    note over Client, Model: Example: The user tries to use a forbidden Nickname or a network timeout occurs

    Client -> Server: addPlayer("Alice", "RED")
    activate Server
    Server -> Controller: addPlayer("Alice", "RED")
    activate Controller
    Controller -> Model: validate request
    activate Model

    Model --> Controller: throws InvalidActionException
    deactivate Model

    Controller --> Server: throws InvalidActionException
    deactivate Controller

    Server --> Client: throws Exception (e.g., RemoteException)
    deactivate Server

    Client -> Client: catch(Exception e)
    User <-- Client: Displays Error Message/Popup\n"Error during creation"

end
deactivate Client

@enduml